An Ansible playbook needs completion on the jump host, where a team member left off. Below are the details:
The inventory file /home/thor/ansible/inventory requires adjustments. The playbook must run on App Server 1 in Stratos DC. Update the inventory accordingly.
Create a playbook /home/thor/ansible/playbook.yml. Include a task to create an empty file /tmp/file.txt on App Server 1.

Note: Validation will run the playbook using the command ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml. Ensure the playbook works without any additional arguments.

SOLUTION

You need two files on the jump host. Since validation runs from /home/thor/ansible, use the following.

1. Check/update the inventory

App Server 1 is stapp01. Your inventory should contain:

[app]
stapp01

If the existing inventory already has connection variables, keep them and only make sure stapp01 is the target host.

2. Create /home/thor/ansible/playbook.yml
---
- name: Create file on App Server 1
  hosts: stapp01
  become: true
  tasks:
    - name: Create empty file
      ansible.builtin.file:
        path: /tmp/file.txt
        state: touch
        mode: '0644'
3. Test it
cd /home/thor/ansible
ansible -i inventory stapp01 -m ping
ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml

Then verify:

ssh stapp01 "ls -l /tmp/file.txt"

You should see /tmp/file.txt on App Server 1 (stapp01).

